#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"runtime-50\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "September 2026 {#september-2026}"
msgstr "September 2026 {#september-2026}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model) offers new tools for inspecting and customizing error mitigation workflow** &mdash; New tools have been built on top of the directed execution model framework, which was released earlier this year:\n"
msgstr "**[Model pelaksanaan terarah](/guides/directed-execution-model) menawarkan alat baharu untuk memeriksa dan menyesuaikan aliran kerja mitigasi ralat** &mdash; Alat baharu telah dibina di atas rangka kerja model pelaksanaan terarah, yang dikeluarkan awal tahun ini:\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Together with [Samplomatic](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/samplomatic/index), they make up the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model), which provides full transparency and control to fine-tune your error mitigation workflow. The [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart) tutorial, for example, demonstrates how this model is used to combine advanced techniques, including shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), and [measurement-based postselection](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks), to further improve the result quality.\n"
"  - [`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) is a toolkit for randomization-based quantum noise characterization. You can use it to construct a custom noise-learning experiment, validate it with local simulation, and analyze the raw results.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Bersama-sama dengan [Samplomatic](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/samplomatic/index), ia membentuk [model pelaksanaan terarah](/guides/directed-execution-model), yang menyediakan ketelusan dan kawalan penuh untuk menyesuaikan aliran kerja mitigasi ralat anda. Tutorial [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart), misalnya, menunjukkan cara model ini digunakan untuk menggabungkan teknik lanjutan, termasuk shaded lightcones, probabilistic error cancellation (PEC), Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX), dan [postselection berasaskan pengukuran](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/postselection-with-non-markovian-error-checks), untuk meningkatkan lagi kualiti hasil.\n"
"  - [`qiskit-noise-learning`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-noise-learning) ialah kit alat untuk pencirian hingar kuantum berasaskan perawakan. Anda boleh menggunakannya untuk membina eksperimen pembelajaran hingar tersuai, mengesahkannya dengan simulasi tempatan, dan menganalisis hasil mentah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) is a package of quantum error mitigation methods for building mitigation pipelines with the new execution model. It includes implementations of well-known methods, including PEC, PEA, TREX, and gate-folding ZNE, as well as post-selection for filtering out non-Markovian errors.\n"
msgstr "[`qiskit-mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/addons/qiskit-mitigation) ialah pakej kaedah mitigasi ralat kuantum untuk membina saluran paip mitigasi dengan model pelaksanaan baharu. Ia merangkumi pelaksanaan kaedah yang terkenal, termasuk PEC, PEA, TREX, dan ZNE gate-folding, serta post-selection untuk menapis ralat bukan-Markov.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes#0500-2026-09-24) released **new client-side implementations of Sampler and Estimator** primitives that are built on top of this framework. These implementations allow you to inspect exactly how each error mitigation method is implemented and test them [locally](/guides/local-testing-mode) before running them on an actual QPU. \n"
msgstr "[`qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/release-notes#0500-2026-09-24) mengeluarkan **pelaksanaan sisi klien yang baharu bagi primitif Sampler dan Estimator** yang dibina di atas rangka kerja ini. Pelaksanaan ini membolehkan anda memeriksa dengan tepat bagaimana setiap kaedah mitigasi ralat dilaksanakan dan mengujinya [secara tempatan](/guides/local-testing-mode) sebelum menjalankannya pada QPU sebenar. \n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    **How to upgrade to the new primitives:** Upgrading to the new primitives is designed to be low-friction, so in most cases, you only need to change your import statements &mdash; not the body of your code. See the [migration guide](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for full details.\n"
msgstr "    **Cara menaik taraf kepada primitif baharu:** Menaik taraf kepada primitif baharu direka supaya mudah, jadi dalam kebanyakan kes, anda hanya perlu menukar penyata import anda &mdash; bukan isi kod anda. Lihat [panduan migrasi](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) untuk butiran lengkap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**New skills for agents** &mdash; Whether you are migrating to the new client-side Sampler and Estimator, or migrating old notebooks that still use V1 primitives, the migrate-qiskit-ibm-runtime skill in the [Qiskit/skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) repository can simplify the task. This new open-source repository contains official, IBM-verified agent skills for building IBM Quantum and Qiskit workflows. We will be adding more skills to this repository in the near future.\n"
msgstr "**Kemahiran baharu untuk ejen** &mdash; Sama ada anda berhijrah ke Sampler dan Estimator sisi klien yang baharu, atau memigrasikan notebook lama yang masih menggunakan primitif V1, kemahiran migrate-qiskit-ibm-runtime dalam repositori [Qiskit/skills](https://github.com/Qiskit/skills) boleh memudahkan tugas ini. Repositori sumber terbuka baharu ini mengandungi kemahiran ejen rasmi yang disahkan IBM untuk membina aliran kerja IBM Quantum dan Qiskit. Kami akan menambah lebih banyak kemahiran ke repositori ini tidak lama lagi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lastly, check out the [PEC with logical noise models tutorial](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-cancellation-with-logical-noise-models) for an example of stacking error detection and mitigation methods using these new tools.\n"
msgstr "Akhir sekali, lihat [tutorial PEC dengan model hingar logik](/tutorials/probabilistic-error-cancellation-with-logical-noise-models) untuk contoh menyusun kaedah pengesanan dan mitigasi ralat menggunakan alat baharu ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-07 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The directed execution model, comprised of [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/) and [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor), exposes the error mitigation logic applied to your workloads so that you have full control over the logic without sacrificing performance.\n"
msgstr "  Model pelaksanaan terarah, yang terdiri daripada [Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/) dan [Executor](/guides/get-started-with-executor), mendedahkan logik mitigasi ralat yang dikenakan pada beban kerja anda supaya anda mempunyai kawalan penuh ke atas logik tersebut tanpa mengorbankan prestasi.\n"

